attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `ydfI`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2% of calls {S1}. The model names 94% of them, at 0.97 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 6 to 85%, in a region of plasticity in 8 to 90% of calls {S2}. A branch of 23 families runs through columns 2 to 24, a parallel path some chromosomes carry instead, 19 persistent and 4 shell, at 10 to 12% {S2.b2}. The `lsr` genes, columns 25 to 32, are [[autoinducer 2 transport]] {S2.c25-33, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 87%, and hesitates more there, 0.97 against 0.71 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 42, `fimC`, is a fork column, at 1.44 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Column 79, `YncO`, is carried by 16% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. The `nar` genes, columns 70 to 73, are [[nitrate reductase]] {S2.c52-73, Q}.

@whole **Across the window it names 87% of genes**, 0.71 bits on average, perplexity 2.0 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.20 against 0.29 bits, and names fewer genes, 78% against 95% {C}.

